# Practice Evidence

Store small, non-sensitive evidence here or link to evidence kept elsewhere.

Useful evidence includes:

- untouched first attempts;
- raw observations, results, scores, or feedback;
- before-and-after work;
- source-backed corrections;
- unaided exercise attempts with their conditions and results;
- deliberate variations;
- diagnosed failures and reruns; and
- capstone evaluation artifacts.

Use dated, descriptive filenames. Keep raw evidence separate from interpretation. Redact personal, confidential, copyrighted, credential, biometric, or otherwise sensitive material. Do not commit large generated artifacts when a reproducible manifest or external link is sufficient.

An absent artifact is not successful evidence. Link each skill status change to the exact supporting item.
